=== 3. WEEK-1 HFA (Theory 5) ===
  HFA at equal ratings: other weeks +2.09 (se 0.22); W1 shift -1.04 (se 0.84, p=0.215)  [2009-2025 non-neutral, n=4059]
  market home residual W1 1999-2025: -0.83 (se 0.64, p=0.197, n=425)  -> consistent sign, not significant: keep site HFA; optional -0.5 W1 haircut (LOW)

=== 4. WEEK-1 TOTAL PRIOR (Theory 3) ===
  realized W1 mean - previous-season mean: -1.32 (se 0.75, p=0.092, 26 seasons)
  realized W1 mean - same-season W2+ mean:  -1.30 (se 0.71, p=0.078); seasons negative 20 of 27 (binomial p=0.019)
  market W1 total residual -0.47 (se 0.64, n=428) vs W5+ +0.76 (se 0.18): W1 - W5+ = -1.23 (Welch p=0.066)
  2025 realized mean total (all REG) = 46.03  -> engine prior 46.0 confirmed; RECOMMENDED 2026 W1 prior = 46.03 - 1.0 = 45.0 (W2+ revert to 46.0)
  rating coefficient c in W1: fit<=2021 c=0.363 (se 0.230) vs engine 0.35 -> keep 0.35 (see 02 log)

=== 5. NEW HEAD COACH / NEW QB IN WEEK 1 (Theory 4) — from 04 log ===
  new HC: W1 resid vs market -0.18 (se 1.11, n=412 games / 171 team-games), ATS 0.493 -> REJECTED, no adjustment
  new starting QB (vs prev-season primary): +2.13 (se 0.98, p=0.03; FIT +2.10, TEST +2.31), back ATS 0.582 (p=0.04), resid vs rating line +1.58 (se 1.13)
  -> W1 only: +1.0 pt toward a team whose planned W1 starter differs from last season's primary starter (half the point estimate); never apply the
     'starter->backup' downgrade to a planned new starter in W1. LOW confidence; re-test after 2026.

